OS reduce-motion and reduce-transparency settings: `App::reduce_transparency`, the platform hook, macOS and iOS.

What:
- Core: `AccessibilityDisplaySettings { reduce_motion, reduce_transparency }`; `Platform::accessibility_display_settings`
  (default: neither) and `Platform::on_accessibility_display_settings_change` (default: no-op). `App::new` takes the
  settings at startup and follows each change through `set_reduce_motion` / the new `set_reduce_transparency`, inside
  an app update so the windows refresh. An OS change wins over an app's own `set_reduce_*` made since.
  `App::reduce_transparency` / `set_reduce_transparency` mirror upstream's `reduce_motion` (no reader in GPUI yet;
  Parallax's materials will read it). The test platform keeps the callback for a table test of the rules.
- gpui_apple: `process_info::observe_notification`, the process info observers' deferred, drop-removed observer for
  a notification from any sender (`with_center` takes the sender to observe).
- macOS: `NSWorkspace` `accessibilityDisplayShouldReduceMotion` / `…ShouldReduceTransparency`, followed through
  `NSWorkspaceAccessibilityDisplayOptionsDidChangeNotification` on the workspace's notification center
  (objc2-app-kit feature `NSAccessibility`).
- iOS: `UIAccessibilityIsReduceMotionEnabled` / `UIAccessibilityIsReduceTransparencyEnabled` and their two
  did-change notifications, as React Native's RCTAccessibilityManager.mm reads and observes them (objc2-ui-kit
  feature `UIAccessibility`). Flutter's FlutterViewController.mm observes the same notifications for its
  accessibility features. Both backends defer the callback to the foreground executor.

Why: upstream's animation element, animated SVGs and animated images obey `App::reduce_motion`, but no platform set
it, so the OS's reduce-motion setting never reached GPUI apps; reduce transparency had no field at all. The platform
trait and `App` are core, so neither a Parallax crate nor an extension trait can add the hook.

Ported from facebook/react-native packages/react-native/React/CoreModules/RCTAccessibilityManager.mm @ v0.88.1
(c30b7f86850d47422637a64c70508e7411dbd8ea), Copyright (c) Meta Platforms, Inc. and affiliates, MIT (the two reads and
notifications, iOS).

Upstream PR: not filed (filing paused, patch rule 14).

